---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';

const contact = SITE.contactEmail ? `mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}` : SITE.issues;
const contactLabel = SITE.contactEmail || 'an issue on GitHub';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy" description="What this website and the live demo collect, and what they do not." og="legal" updated="12 November 2026">
  <p>
    This page covers the {SITE.name} website and the live demo. It does not cover a {SITE.name} install that you or someone else runs:
    that install is controlled by whoever runs it, and the data in it never comes to us.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No cookies.</strong> The site sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser to track you.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Visit counts without tracking you.</strong> When analytics is on, it counts page views and a few clicks, such as starting an
      install, with a cookie-free tool. It does not build a profile of you or follow you to other sites.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> The service that serves the site keeps short-lived logs, including addresses, to keep it running and
      stop abuse.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The live demo</h2>
  <p>
    When it is available, the demo creates a temporary project for you without an account. Whatever you enter there is deleted, with the
    project and the account made for you, after 24 hours. The demo sends no email and does not connect to other services. Please do not
    enter real personal data.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Starting a demo shows a check from <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>, which keeps
      automated sign-ups out. Cloudflare sees your address and some details of your browser to do this, under its
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>To limit how many demos one address can start, a hashed form of your address is kept for an hour, then deleted. It is not stored anywhere else.</li>
    <li>The demo dashboard uses one cookie to keep you signed in to your demo. It ends when the demo is deleted.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The open-source software</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} itself sends nothing to us. It has no telemetry and does not call home, and the data it stores stays in your own
    database.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy: <a href={contact}>{contactLabel}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
